# The app is its own 404 page.
#
# Anything that is not a real file is served index.html with a 404 status, and
# main.js works out from the URL that it is not at home and opens a blank board
# whose ghost cards say so (see notFound in main.js, NOTFOUND in state.js).
#
# The status is not optional and is the whole reason this is a rule rather than
# a rewrite. A 200 here would be a soft 404: a page saying "not found" while
# telling every crawler it is fine, which is how dead addresses end up indexed.
#
# This file is the Netlify / Cloudflare Pages spelling. serve.py does the same
# thing for local development. A host that only understands a literal 404.html
# - GitHub Pages is the one that matters - cannot express this, and would need
# that file to be a copy of index.html instead.

/*    /index.html    404
